___________________________________________________
Terminal Command in MAC 

private-ip:      ifconfig | grep 'inet '
                 (this shows all the network interfaces; 'if' means 'i f' that is interface, and config means configuration)
                 (it also shows the subnet mask id)
                 (en:   ethernet interface (wifi or cable))
                 (utun: user-tunnel (VPN))
public-ip:       curl ifconfig.me  
                 (curl is an https request command that prints whatever the website (ifconfig.me or www.google.com) returns)
gateway-ip:      route -n get default
                 (n: means numeric)
